  "full_text": "This is Luso's 64-bit operating system for the IBM PC that's free and open source. It's designed for recreational programming. I wrote Luso's over the past 8 years. It's 130,000 lines of code and it never executes code I didn't write. That means it doesn't do libraries or modules or anything. It just does a couple BIOS calls. Anyway, it's 64-bit and it includes a kernel, a compiler, an assembler, an unassembler, a debugger, an editor, a graphics library, a GUI, and tools like grep and merge, and tons and tons of demos. In fact, we're going to look at some of the demos that come with it here in a sec. And that turns into that Thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.",
